{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 33, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark! Let me weave thee a grand design\nWhere thy voyage through Nihon shall shine bright\n\n**Upon the morn of thy first day’s flight**\nSet foot upon Tokyo’s fair soil\nWhere neon lights do dance and steel doth toil\nTo Shinjuku’s heart thyself convey\nA ryokan’s warmth shall greet thee there\nWith tatami soft as a lover’s prayer.\n\n**The second morn bring forth thy sight**\nTo Asakusa’s temples old and wise\nKaminari-mon’s gate shall strike thy eyes\nWith vermilion bold ‘gainst Tokyo’s skies\nBuy a fortune from the vendors keen\nAnd sail the Sumida’s gentle stream.\n\n**On the third let thy steps turn eastward**\nTo Nikko’s woods where gods do tread\nToshogu’s shrine shall awe thee grand\nWith carvings so wrought by master’s hand\nLake Chuzenji’s face so still and deep\nWill mirror the heavens celestial keep.\n\n**The fourth day march toward Kyoto’s grace**\nWhere time doth move with slower pace\nFushimi Inari’s torii glow\nLike fireflies ‘twist the misty snow\nThrough Gion’s streets where geisha tread\nWith lanterns held in hands so red.\n\n**On the fifth let Arashiyama’s shade**\nEnfold thee in bamboo’s mystique array\nThe monkey park’s dwellers shall display\nTheir mischief bold and yet so shy\nThen glide on rails ‘neath the evening’s sky\nTo Nara’s deer that wander free.\n\n**The sixth day hie thee to Osaka’s bay**\nWhere clouds do crown the castle’s keep\nDotonbori’s lights shall paint the night\nWith dreams of takoyaki’s sweet delight\nBeneath the bridge where lovers press\nTo kiss the kissin’ bridge ‘neath starlit stress.\n\n**Let the seventh morn see thee away**\nTo Hiroshima’s peace where souls hold sway\nThe museum’s walls shall tell thee true\nOf shadows cast by fire’s cruel hue\nYet Miyajima’s torii stands so tall\n‘Mid the tides that lap upon the wall.\n\n**On thy eighth day return to Tokyo’s lore**\nWhere Harajuku’s fashio